{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1546999-idea-for-a-story","id":1546999,"title":"Idea for a story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-14T14:07:03-08:00","id":1546999,"title":"Idea for a story","content":"Your pack of Werewolves is sent to destroy a coastal Pentex facility belonging to Project Deepwater. You are accompanied by two local Fera guides, one Rokea and one Mokele. However, the facility not only has First Teams and corrupt Technocracy &quot;scientists&quot; under their employ but also Chulorviah, Mariner Gangrel, Scuttlers, Anurana and Balefire Sharks stalk the tainted waters around the Facility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-14-2024, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T14:14:24-08:00","id":1547001,"title":"","content":"So a story idea for very high level characters where a single pack with two helper NPCs are expected to take that down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T14:18:29-08:00","id":1547003,"title":"","content":"Yup! Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T17:52:26-08:00","id":1547012,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that this could be done by a group like that. Also, remember that Pentex facilities are typically guarded by multiple First Teams according to the Freak Legion book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 12-14-2024, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T18:56:05-08:00","id":1547015,"title":"","content":"With that many heavy hitters in residence your gonna need a bigger boat, to place some calls to Black Eagle and Dies Ultima, call in favours with the local GW Sept allied with Clashing Boom Boom and get those Rokea and Mokole to get their Wallow and multiple Slews involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T19:12:10-08:00","id":1547017,"title":"","content":"The First Teams will be either a Company or a Battalion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-16-2024, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T19:42:22-08:00","id":1547019,"title":"","content":"ajsjcn da,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","user":"Psicose","date":".  Wrong place. 12-14-2024, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T19:47:16-08:00","id":1547021,"title":"","content":"What does that mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T20:20:04-08:00","id":1547023,"title":"","content":"How about this? Swap Mokole for a Corax who will be responsible for watching the area from above, so the pack has an idea of \u200bthe general area and can alert them in case of an emergency, Rokea stays with them to provide muscle support. As for the enemies, it makes sense that they would be related to the sea, but I think it can be more practical. They first have to enter through a sea route, with a boat or hidden in a Pentex cargo ship, in which case the route would be guarded by several Churloviah who in theory would only cause problems in groups and a small group of Balefire Sharks, to accompany them who would be more difficult to face.<br /> <br /> Once infiltrated, we enter the land part, in this case I advise going for the basics, well-armed and equipped Pentex guards and some BSD, nothing too prominent in this part unless you want to make an enemy more memorable. Moving on to the destruction of the base, we can go in two ways. The first would be for the pack to tamper with some central control system to overheat the installation or flood it. The second would be to place bombs at strategic points. I recommend the second one because this would allow for complications at each of the strategic points previously mentioned but if you prefer a quicker thing the first could be better.<br /> <br /> For the last phase, there is the exit. Basically, the pack has to escape from an exploding or flooding base, but naturally something will get in the way. What to do here will depend on the escape strategy. One possibility is to try to escape along the coast by taking a boat. In this case, you can choose to put several enemies in the way or corner them at sea with a larger enemy. Another would be to escape through the sky with a helicopter, In this case, there is not much to do, just go with the flow. Finally, there would be an escape through the Umbra. In this case, it would be a good idea to make it interesting with something waiting for them inside, something like a final boss type of enemy.<br /> <br /> Now, this was a base structure, Some other ideas you could include would be:<br /> <br /> <br /> - An alternative entrance would be to enter through a sewer pipe, which could be guarded by Anurana or even be their nest (?).<br /> <br /> - I mentioned that it would be good to include BSD, but you don't have to limit yourself to just Garou. Add a Gurahl, Mokole or even Yeren if you think that would make the situation more interesting.<br /> <br /> - You had the idea of \u200b\u200bincluding Marine Gangrel, but I think that instead of including several, you could include just one elder and give him the ability to transform into a sea chimera, which could even hinder the escape or be a mere obstacle, if you prefer.<br /> <br /> - If you want to add drama, you can include that a kinfolk or Rokea's romantic partner was captured and is being held inside the facility. If you like tragedy, he could be corrupted and become a fomori.<br /> <br /> - I already mentioned Corax, but one idea that could work is to have him get hit by a bullet or captured by a vulture during the confusion and the group would be forced to go out of their way to go after him or split up the group, this could give an interesting outcome.<br /> <br /> - If you go with the helicopter ending, you could put in a part where a creature hangs up there with them or something manages to knock the helicopter down and the pack is forced to make an emergency landing.<br /> <br /> I hope this could help some way.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T06:27:04-08:00","id":1547026,"title":"","content":"The reason I chose the Mokole as a guide was because it's a Saltwater Crocodile who is personally affected by the facility's presence. Now that you mention sewers maybe there could be some Renegade Freakfeet in the sewer system as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-15-2024, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T13:14:39-08:00","id":1547036,"title":"","content":"The &quot;corrupt Technocracy scientists&quot; are full blown infiltrated Nephandi or just unaware unethical employees?<br /> <br /> It actually makes a lot of difference if they are part of the secret demonic cult or if they're just gullible unwilling participants. And how many of them are there, what's their capabilities?<br /> <br /> Also remember, if there are Technocrats involved, expect retaliation from the Union, unless the party can leave evidence of their corruption for when the MiB shows up.<br /> <br /> If they are just dupes, they could be convinced to, if not actively help, then to at least stand aside. <br /> <br /> This could end up being resolved &quot;diplomatically&quot; (a downer I know), but on the other hand thou if they are actual infiltrated Nephandi, trying to contact them would blew it all over.<br /> <br /> Just to add a few complications to make things more interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T14:24:29-08:00","id":1547044,"title":"","content":"I was thinking they could be either one, Nephandi or unaware unethical employees. And as for what groups they're from they could be Void Engineers, Progenitors or Iteration X technicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-15-2024, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-15T19:49:47-08:00","id":1547047,"title":"","content":"My main concern is that with the number and composition of opponents you've listed your going to need both high Rank and high numbers to have even the possibility of success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T07:11:01-08:00","id":1547057,"title":"","content":"So, you're saying that even with a Pack, a Wallow and a Slew they can't easily deal with Scuttlers, a First Team Company, a Mariner Gangrel, a couple Chulorviah and a small group of Balefire Sharks and Anurana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-16-2024, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T12:01:58-08:00","id":1547063,"title":"","content":"Remember, First Team Members could be Humans, Fomori, Vampires, Mages and Black Spiral Dancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T13:22:59-08:00","id":1547065,"title":"","content":"From what I've researched, a first team for a platoon would have an average of 20 to 30 members. If they are made up of only humans, it is possible to defeat them with time, but if there are other creatures in the middle, then it will depend on a lot of things. Now, if it is a battalion, it can vary from 500 to 800 enemies, it is a lot to deal with. Can you be more specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T13:49:52-08:00","id":1547068,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, it would probably be a Company or a Battalion. So maybe to make things easier it would be a Company with maybe 20 fomori and the rest are humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T13:52:47-08:00","id":1547070,"title":"","content":"So, that would make it a First Team Company of 20 fomori and 60 humans led by a human Captain. A few Technocracy technicians, some Scuttlers in the Umbra, a Mariner Gangrel, a couple Chulorviah and a small group of Balefire Sharks. A few Anurana and maybe some Renegade Freakfeet in the Sewer System.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  Details 12-16-2024, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T14:55:18-08:00","id":1547075,"title":"","content":"I think you're vastly underestimating how much numbers matter in conflicts in the WoD when actually running the game (though this is purposeful design).<br /> <br /> The supernatural, even tough beasties like the Garou, are supposed to be afraid of humanity. Not individual humans, a human or a handful of humans are easily dealt with. When you start getting into large numbers (and potential supernatural aid like Technocrats providing protection from Delirium), 60 humans with modern range weapons arranged efficiently will just mow down the Garou in a stand up fight. Most supernaturals are (at least until very high XP) are designed to be able to be overwhelmed by sheer numbers of human combatants. This is a major impetus for the supernatural to keep itself hidden even with magical effects enforcing that further: humanity would win - or at least ensure MAD - with the power of more bodies to throw at the conflict.<br /> <br /> The more antagonists, just in terms of how many of them can attack the PCs at once and even in waves without rest, the deadlier the encounter gets for the PCs. It's one of the worst situations to put PCs in because WoD PCs have very limited resources that don't get regained quickly on demand. 10 Rage, 10 Gnosis, and 10 Willpower is not a lot when you're facing a small army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T15:33:58-08:00","id":1547077,"title":"","content":"I was trying to be faithful to the lore. Important facilities would be guarded by a small army. And Werewolves are pretty OP especially a pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  details 12-16-2024, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T17:38:24-08:00","id":1547080,"title":"","content":"The reflects the danger Garou represent... but that's why the Garou can field their own armies when necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T18:20:40-08:00","id":1547081,"title":"","content":"Well, in that case you should have your guides bring their wallow and slew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T20:11:06-08:00","id":1547086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1546999-idea-for-a-story?p=1547080#post1547080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reflects the danger Garou represent... but that's why the Garou can field their own armies when necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that, they would also face threats of such a magnitude with intelligence gathering and with tactics, not blindly charging at it. An attack on such a facility would take months of preparations and Intel gathering smaller missions.<br /> <br /> A successful attack could mean removing some of the threats ahead of the siege - for example, managing to relocate the Technocrats, causing a false alarm somewhere else that causes those 60 humans to be deployed somewhere else and some such.<br /> <br /> The attack could be considered a total failure at that assessment period, before the siege or any fight at all happens, in case of exposure or if the would be attackers, after gathering enough Intel, come to the conclusion that it is above their resources even with all planing in the world (but they might still try to recruit additional aid from others that might be able to fill that gap).<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T12:12:35-08:00","id":1547112,"title":"","content":"So, the addition of an entire wallow, a slew and a Corax wouldn't make a difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T12:49:29-08:00","id":1547114,"title":"","content":"I think the bigger issue is scenario escalation. By adding every potential antagonist under the waves to the initial idea, you've escalated the level of threat the enemy facility represents. So the PCs have to escalate their resources in return, and all of this presumes something important enough that the enemy will want to try to counter-escalate if they come under attack (corrupt Technocrats can operate teleporters, BSDs can open Moonbridges to get allies there within minutes from hundreds or thousands of miles away, etc.).<br /> <br /> This is basically how the canonical war in the Amazon grew so big: instead of a quick &quot;Garou come in and wreck the Wyrm with a bit of Fera help,&quot; it turned into an entrenched conflict as the Wyrm's forces were willing to throw a lot at keeping their position, and the Garou and their allies weren't ready to give up either.<br /> <br /> If that's what you want to have happen, that's cool, the War in the Amazon was a prominent feature in the original run of the game. If that's not what you're looking for, you need to figure out what kind of scale you really want out of this and then pick the antagonists to fit (even if that potentially means cutting some of the variety or numbers of them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T14:02:18-08:00","id":1547115,"title":"","content":"Well, I never said there would be Black Spiral Dancers there. Also, like I said before I was trying to be Lore accurate, Project Deepwater has ties to the Technocracy and Important facilities tend to have a small army guarding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T16:44:31-08:00","id":1547118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1546999-idea-for-a-story?p=1547115#post1547115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I never said there would be Black Spiral Dancers there. Also, like I said before I was trying to be Lore accurate, Project Deepwater has ties to the Technocracy and Important facilities tend to have a small army guarding them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it can have ties with the Technocrats, but that doesn't mean that every Technocrat holding is a fortress with its own small army.<br /> <br /> It can be if you wish it to be, but then like Heavy Arms has said, it wouldn't just be a matter of getting in and getting out. This would need careful planning and months of it. Which means that the opposition has a big chance of catching wind of it and both starting to hunt the hunters, and fortifying even further.<br /> <br /> This is like the paradox of security in geopolitics. If I'm afraid to be attacked, I'll build more weapons. But then, my neighbors will feel threatened by my accumulation of weapons, and they'll feel the need to raise their armies, which in turn will make me even more afraid, pushing my nation to build even more weapons, and on and on in a cycle.<br /> <br /> The PCs would probably need to escalate things, trying to recruit packs to the cause, and the more it grows, the harder it gets to keep things secret. Which means that the opposition has a chance to do the same, when they realize that there's an imminent threat.<br /> <br /> This can be exploitable thou: resources aren't infinite for neither side. Which means that, if the opposition is pulling resources to that facility, other places will become more vulnerable. One way to exploit this could be by doing small raids on the surrounding, to attract the enemies to it, and then attacking OTHER facilities which, while may be less important targets, could still represent important victories.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the enemy won't just play defense, and they'll start to fight back. And since the Garou's resources aren't infinite either, this means that many small Caerns would be vulnerable to attacks.<br /> <br /> One way to deal with this would be with massive numbers, and screw planning. Instead of months of planning, the PCs manage a shitton of packs to participate in a huge lightning raid. While this has the downside of meaning &quot;going in the dark&quot;, it has the positive side of not giving the opposition the chance to set countermeasures. Besides, it would lead to some fun sessions about politics and diplomacy and lots of social interaction before ending it with a massive bang and a furious battle. And with massive numbers, you could just overwhelm the enemy quickly before they can react, thus minimizing losses. The real challenge in this would be to manage to actually assemble such a powerful force.<br /> <br /> The other positive side is that this would be the path with the least chance of igniting an open war against the entirety of the Technocracy, instead of just the Wyrm corrupt elements of it. It Pentex loses a facility in a quick raid, they'll most likely hide most of it from the rest of the Union; if this drags on however, other conventions can unaware be thrown into the fight by the corrupt parties, thus leading to a much bigger and unnecessary fight at the hands of the Garou.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can reduce the scope of things if you're not trying to do some Rage on Amazon stuff or the Atomic War in Doissetep. Thus, you could have the facility filled with human security and half a dozen Fomori, which would still be quite the fight for a single pack of PCs, but without all the rest of Vampires and Nephandic Mages and Technocrats and corrupted Fera.<br /> <br /> It is up to you how to go about it thou. I think that a game of high politics to assemble a massive alliance ending with an epic battle and a crazy &quot;all in&quot; raid would be super fun, several sessions of &quot;mission impossible&quot; recon stealth missions and bureaucracy analysis of documents culminating in a precise strike is also fun, but a smaller quick raid would also be cool. Just be sure that you fully understand what each one of the possibilities entail and go for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T17:41:05-08:00","id":1547124,"title":"","content":"I was saying that Pentex has small armies guarding their more important facilities. I would go about information gathering with help from kinfolk and maybe a Corax. Then a stealthy infiltration to sabotage the facility doing as much damage as possible. All out violence is only as a last resort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-22T14:12:03-08:00","id":1547190,"title":"","content":"Also, doesn't Pentex already have a drug that makes people immune to the Delirium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}